module std.resource_contract

// THE CLOSED VALUES A `resource` DECLARATION'S `kind:` AND `mode:` ENTRIES TAKE. Homed in their own
// import-free module rather than in std.resources because the v2 compiler reads them
// (v2.std.resource_declaration) and the compiler's closure is emitted to Rust: importing std.resources
// would pull std.filesystem, std.measure and the rest of its imports into that closure for two enums.
// std.resources imports them, so a declaration there names them in scope.

// These are the homes the v2 lowering reads a declaration's entries against
// (v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_resource_decl), so an unknown value refuses at its entry
// instead of riding as an unclassified name. A Capability is held and used; an Observation is read
// from the world without being held (Clock, Entropy).
type ResourceKind
  = Capability
  | Observation

type ResourceMode
  = Read
  | ReadWrite
